      "name": "VZV Leading Pedestrian Interval Signals",
      "description": "Intersections where DOT installs signals that show a walk sign for pedestrians before showing a green light to vehicle traffic. The goal of these signals is to improve street safety by giving pedestrians a chance to establish their presence in the crosswalk before vehicles make turns across that crosswalk.\r\n\r\nFor a complete list of Vision Zero maps, please follow <a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/browse?q=vzv&sortBy=last_modified&utf8=%E2%9C%93\">this link</a>",
